  "author": "Dr. Lurie",
  "deck": "Most under-eye darkness is not a sleep problem. Here is what is going on underneath, and what the evidence supports doing about it.",
  "description": "Dark circles under the eyes usually come from three overlapping causes: pigment, blood vessels, and shadow. What each looks like, what the evidence supports, and when to see a clinician.",
  "editorial": {
    "framework": "fw_concern",
    "writer_notes": "TOP-stage concern explainer. Dials held well under the site ceiling: claim_strength ~0.14, urgency 0.00, emotional_agitation ~0.04, cta_density ~0.06. One ask only, and it is the next article."
  },
  "image": {
    "alt": "A bathroom mirror in early morning daylight, with a folded linen towel and a glass of water on the counter below.",
    "src": "/img/req_plugin_dark_circles_20260904_01/224094aea5e2d1a94144bf8d84a454a993438f05bc02b378469278d099b42761.webp"
